  "id": "Compound::DB00528 - Gene::1551",
  "verbalization": "Lercanidipine is shown to bind to multiple cytochrome P450 enzymes, including Cyp3a4, Cyp3a5, and Cyp2d6, all of which participate in the same biological pathway involving aromatase activity. This pathway is ultimately linked to Cyp3a7, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Lercanidipine may influence Cyp3a7 function. The shared involvement of these enzymes in aromatase activity implies that Lercanidipine could modulate the activity of Cyp3a7 through a common downstream effect. The evidence suggests that Lercanidipine may exert its effects on Cyp3a7 by inhibiting or modulating the activity of its upstream targets, which in turn could alter the expression or function of Cyp3a7. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Lercanidipine and Cyp3a7, particularly through the involvement of aromatase activity as a central mediator.",
